values ('f6a7b8c9-0d1e-4f58-9c78-8d9e0f1a2b48', 'modern-and-contemporary-art', 'Modern and Contemporary Art', 'Students begin with why modern art emerged from industrialization, colonial modernity, urban life, photography, and new models of perception, then follow the shift from illusionistic representation toward fragmented form, abstraction, and artistic self-consciousness, including Dada, Surrealism, design, and modern media. Later work covers postwar abstraction, Pop, mass culture, Minimalism, Conceptual art, expanded media, feminist, queer, Black, Indigenous, and decolonial histories, identity and the body, global circuits, institutions and markets, public and activist practice, and twenty-first-century digital, ecological, and networked art, with art writing and a comparative research capstone.');

